      "description": "Watch Iceland vs Estonia highlights and goals from UEFA Nations League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 26, 2026. The UEFA Nations League brought Iceland and Estonia together on September 26, 2026, for a match defined by tactical shifts and sudden bursts of drama. Both nations entered the contest seeking momentum, setting the stage for a compelling encounter under the lights. Late First Half Breakthrough The opening period was largely a cagey affair, complicated by an early tactical adjustment for the hosts when Albert Gudmundsson was replaced by Isak Snaer Thorvaldsson in the 30th minute. However, just as the first half reached its conclusion, Iceland found the breakthrough they craved. In the 45th minute, Hakon Arnar Haraldsson turned provider for Andri Gudjohnsen , who clinical finish sent the home side into the break with a slender lead and the wind in their sails. Penalty Miss and Estonian Resilience The second half began with a moment that could have changed everything. In the 52nd minute, Estonia was awarded a penalty, but Kevor Palumets saw his effort go begging, missing a golden chance to level the scores. The visitors refused to let their heads drop, despite Karol Mets picking up a yellow card shortly after. Their persistence was rewarded in the 64th minute when Rasmus Peetson delivered a precise assist for Maksim Paskotsi , who fired home to bring the scores level and ignite the traveling support. A Tense Finish to the Contest As the clock ticked down, both managers turned to their benches to find a winner. Iceland introduced the experienced Gylfi Sigurdsson and Arnor Sigurdsson , while Estonia made several defensive adjustments. The match grew increasingly physical, with yellow cards shown to Rasmus Peetson and Stefan Thordarson as the intensity peaked. Despite five minutes of added time, neither side could find a decisive blow, and the referee’s final whistle confirmed a hard-fought draw between two determined sides."
